{"id": "EUVD-2026-105095", "enisaUuid": "7f357548-257d-34f0-a304-27cbb4b38c37", "description": "HarfBuzz 8.0.0 through 14.6.0 contains an out-of-bounds write vulnerability in the experimental WebAssembly shaper because the font_glyph_to_string import has a wrong WAMR signature. Attackers can supply a crafted font whose wasm module places the output buffer near linear memory's end, writing glyph-name bytes into host memory to crash or corrupt applications.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T16:21:50", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz/pull/6414", "https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz/commit/5e821de8256d01780566b5c8ab7886fae4c93da8", "https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz/blob/14.6.0/src/hb-wasm-api-list.hh#L85", "https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz/blob/14.6.0/src/hb-wasm-api-font.hh#L115-L123", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/harfbuzz-8.0.0-through-14.6.0-out-of-bounds-write-via-webassembly-font-glyph-to-string"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hqgm-v7cx-mq25", "CVE-2026-113679"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "eb2a3c4a-0bfd-3ba1-aa1e-157af04618db", "product": {"name": "harfbuzz", "vendor": {"name": "harfbuzz"}}, "product_version": "8.0.0 \u226414.6.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6c17b773-8921-3f96-aa4b-f2d3083db21b", "vendor": {"name": "harfbuzz"}}], "isExploited": false}